<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Richard Clement Moody</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1813–1887</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Richard Clement Moody was a British officer of the Royal Engineers who served as the first governor of the Falkland Islands from 1841 to 1848. In 1858 he led the Columbia Detachment of Royal Engineers to the new colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-columbia">British Columbia</a>, where as chief commissioner of lands and works he surveyed the country, laid out roads and chose the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-westminster">New Westminster</a> as the capital. He returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1863.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/richard-clement-moody.jpg" alt="Richard Clement Moody" width="284" height="493" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographerUnknown photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Richard_Clement_Moody_(1859).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
